---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Contributing — Machine Authority Protocol" description="How to contribute to the Machine Authority Protocol specification.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero-text">
      <h1>Contributing</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Read the specifications. File issues. Submit PRs.</p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Channels</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Issues:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/yazcaleb/machineauthority-protocol/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/yazcaleb/machineauthority-protocol/issues</a> &mdash; bugs, spec ambiguities, proposed changes.</li>
        <li><strong>Discussions:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/yazcaleb/machineauthority-protocol/discussions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/yazcaleb/machineauthority-protocol/discussions</a> &mdash; async design conversations. Lower barrier than PRs.</li>
        <li><strong>Pull requests:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/yazcaleb/machineauthority-protocol/pulls" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/yazcaleb/machineauthority-protocol/pulls</a> &mdash; spec text, schemas, examples, tooling.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Contribution areas</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Independent implementations</strong> &mdash; v1.0 has one reference implementation (Node, in <code>reference/</code>). A second independent implementation in any language is the highest-value contribution. Use <code>test-vectors/</code> as the conformance bar.</li>
        <li><strong>Test vectors</strong> &mdash; new <code>valid/</code> and <code>invalid/</code> cases for canonicalization, CAR, decision envelope, elicitation loop, and CAC. Each invalid vector must declare its expected verdict per the verifier-CLI contract in <code>CONFORMANCE.md</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Bindings &amp; integrations</strong> &mdash; OPA / Cedar / OpenFGA policy adapters, MCP server middleware, SPIFFE / DID identity binders, Sigstore (Rekor) profile for <code>MAP-CAC-DSSE-1</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Spec ambiguities</strong> &mdash; if two readings of any v1.0 normative MUST are possible, file an issue. Spec text under v1.0 stability is fixed for 12 months; clarifying errata is the path.</li>
        <li><strong>Post-v1.0 roadmap</strong> &mdash; multi-approver quorum, polling profile for the loop, ML-DSA hybrid signatures, transparency-log profile, revocation discovery. Discussions are open; no normative changes until the next major version.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Legal</h2>
      <p>All contributors must sign off commits with the <a href="https://developercertificate.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Developer Certificate of Origin</a> (DCO): <code>git commit -s</code>.</p>
      <p>The specification and this website are MIT-licensed. Reference implementations MAY use any OSI-approved license; MIT or Apache&nbsp;2.0 is recommended.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
